§ `I1: the words that cite s 6ל(א) cite a number that stands for a note`

-- 1. The citing words point at what the target is (the words say the text of a section about the owners' representative; the target is a note that the section was re-marked).
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite s 6ל(א)`)
-- 2. The target has the one section that the citing words name (it has 0 of 1).
#ASSERT `the target has everything the citing words name` (`reference: s 21ב(ג), the words that cite s 6ל(א)`)
-- 3. The number the words cite is the number the section now bears (6ל is cited; the instrument gave the section the number 21ג).
#ASSERT `the number the words cite is the number the section now bears` (`re-marking: s 6ל re-marked 21ג, SH 1807 p. 551`)

§ `I2: the words that cite s 6יב2(1) cite a section that was repealed`

-- 4. The citing words point at what the target is (the words say the text of a paragraph; the target is a section repealed by another instrument).
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 6ח4(ב), the words that cite s 6יב2(1)`)
-- 5. The target has the one paragraph that the citing words name (it has 0 of 1).
#ASSERT `the target has everything the citing words name` (`reference: s 6ח4(ב), the words that cite s 6יב2(1)`)
-- 6. The section the words cite stands outside the numbers the repealing section lists (6יב2 lies inside 6יב1 to 6יב4).
#ASSERT `the section cited stands outside the repealed numbers` (`repeal: ss 6יב1 to 6יב4 repealed, SH 2985 p. 947`)
